# Cloudflare wrangler reads this file when packaging static assets
# for the Workers/Pages deploy pipeline. It works the same way as
# .gitignore — patterns listed here are excluded from the asset
# upload. Empty file means: upload everything in public/.
#
# Cloudflare Pages auto-runs `astro add cloudflare` on Astro projects
# during the deploy step, which configures the project to use the
# Workers asset pipeline. That pipeline requires this file to exist
# (it's an error, not a warning, if it's missing) — hence the empty
# placeholder. If we ever want to exclude an asset from publication
# (a draft PNG, an internal CSS file, etc.), list its pattern here.
